{"artifact_id":"extract_6c9948d99ca7c227eb723309","byte_end":60979,"byte_start":59929,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S3.p7.2","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">In simulation, the string scale <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\text{S}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>S</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\text{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> is varied from 1 to 4<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.2.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>in 0.5<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.2.2\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>steps. For each mass value, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"g_{\\text{S}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mtext>S</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_{\\text{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> values of 0.2, 0.3, and 0.4 are used, while the minimum mass of SBs ranges from 7 to 12<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.2.3\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>in steps of 1<span id=\"Ch0.S3.p7.2.4\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\TeV</span>. These parameter ranges cover both the formation of SBs and their transition to semiclassical BHs.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}